    "conclusion": "The two runs reproduce the same ordering: connection-pool admission is negligible, while batch queue wait and the PostgreSQL worker dominate. Within the worker, the materialized validation read, mutation CTE, and transaction commit are the largest measured SQL segments. The apparent 3.46% throughput advantage over v120/v121 is diagnostic only because the stage selection changed and both runs fail the unchanged stability gate. Optimize one SQL hypothesis at a time and re-run the same stage set before retaining any change."
